    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i need help writing a rejection email for a candidate. They made it to the final round for a senior dev role here in Austin, so it's a tough one. They were really strong in system design and had great culture fit, but we just went with someone who had a bit more experience with our specific cloud stack. Can you draft something professional and kind so we don't burn a bridge?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can help you craft a rejection email that's both professional and kind. Here's a draft:\n\nDear [Candidate Name],\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the status of your application for the Senior Developer position at [Company Name]. We were truly impressed by your exceptional skills in system design and your alignment with our company culture. However, after careful consideration, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose experience with our specific cloud stack aligns more closely with our current needs.\n\nPlease know that this decision was not made lightly, and we were genuinely excited about the prospect of having you join our team. Your passion for system design and commitment to delivering high-quality solutions are truly admirable, and we have no doubt that you will find a role that leverages your talents.\n\nWe appreciate the time and effort you invested in our hiring process, and we're grateful for the opportunity to have had you as a finalist. We wish you all the best in your job search and hope that our paths will cross again in the future.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name]\n\nI hope this draft captures the tone you're looking for. You can always modify it to fit your company's voice and style. Remember, it's essential to be kind and gracious",
